{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-john-007",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 7,
  "title": "John 7",
  "display_title": "John 7",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "john",
  "book": "John",
  "bookName": "John",
  "bookOrder": 43,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 7,
  "sortOrder": 43007,
  "verseCount": 53,
  "aliases": [
    "John",
    "Jn",
    "Jhn"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "After these things Jesus walked in Galilee: for he would not walk in Jewry, because the Jews sought to kill him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Now the Jews’ feast of tabernacles was at hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "His brethren therefore said unto him, Depart hence, and go into Judaea, that thy disciples also may see the works that thou doest.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For there is no man that doeth any thing in secret, and he himself seeketh to be known openly. If thou do these things, shew thyself to the world.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For neither did his brethren believe in him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Then Jesus said unto them, My time is not yet come: but your time is alway ready.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "The world cannot hate you; but me it hateth, because I testify of it, that the works thereof are evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Go ye up unto this feast: I go not up yet unto this feast: for my time is not yet full come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "When he had said these words unto them, he abode still in Galilee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But when his brethren were gone up, then went he also up unto the feast, not openly, but as it were in secret.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Then the Jews sought him at the feast, and said, Where is he?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And there was much murmuring among the people concerning him: for some said, He is a good man: others said, Nay; but he deceiveth the people.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Howbeit no man spake openly of him for fear of the Jews.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Now about the midst of the feast Jesus went up into the temple, and taught.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And the Jews marvelled, saying, How knoweth this man letters, having never learned?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Jesus answered them, and said, My doctrine is not mine, but his that sent me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "If any man will do his will, he shall know of the doctrine, whether it be of God, or whether I speak of myself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "He that speaketh of himself seeketh his own glory: but he that seeketh his glory that sent him, the same is true, and no unrighteousness is in him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Did not Moses give you the law, and yet none of you keepeth the law? Why go ye about to kill me?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "The people answered and said, Thou hast a devil: who goeth about to kill thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Jesus answered and said unto them, I have done one work, and ye all marvel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Moses therefore gave unto you circumcision; (not because it is of Moses, but of the fathers;) and ye on the sabbath day circumcise a man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "If a man on the sabbath day receive circumcision, that the law of Moses should not be broken; are ye angry at me, because I have made a man every whit whole on the sabbath day?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Judge not according to the appearance, but judge righteous judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Then said some of them of Jerusalem, Is not this he, whom they seek to kill?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "But, lo, he speaketh boldly, and they say nothing unto him. Do the rulers know indeed that this is the very Christ?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Howbeit we know this man whence he is: but when Christ cometh, no man knoweth whence he is.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Then cried Jesus in the temple as he taught, saying, Ye both know me, and ye know whence I am: and I am not come of myself, but he that sent me is true, whom ye know not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "But I know him: for I am from him, and he hath sent me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Then they sought to take him: but no man laid hands on him, because his hour was not yet come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "And many of the people believed on him, and said, When Christ cometh, will he do more miracles than these which this man hath done?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "The Pharisees heard that the people murmured such things concerning him; and the Pharisees and the chief priests sent officers to take him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Then said Jesus unto them, Yet a little while am I with you, and then I go unto him that sent me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Ye shall seek me, and shall not find me: and where I am, thither ye cannot come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "Then said the Jews among themselves, Whither will he go, that we shall not find him? will he go unto the dispersed among the Gentiles, and teach the Gentiles?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "What manner of saying is this that he said, Ye shall seek me, and shall not find me: and where I am, thither ye cannot come?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "In the last day, that great day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "(But this spake he of the Spirit, which they that believe on him should receive: for the Holy Ghost was not yet given; because that Jesus was not yet glorified.)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-040",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 40,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:40",
      "numberLabel": "40",
      "text": "Many of the people therefore, when they heard this saying, said, Of a truth this is the Prophet.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:40",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:40"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-041",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 41,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:41",
      "numberLabel": "41",
      "text": "Others said, This is the Christ. But some said, Shall Christ come out of Galilee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:41",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-042",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 42,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:42",
      "numberLabel": "42",
      "text": "Hath not the scripture said, That Christ cometh of the seed of David, and out of the town of Bethlehem, where David was?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:42",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:42"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-043",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 43,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:43",
      "numberLabel": "43",
      "text": "So there was a division among the people because of him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:43",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-044",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 44,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:44",
      "numberLabel": "44",
      "text": "And some of them would have taken him; but no man laid hands on him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:44",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:44"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-045",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 45,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:45",
      "numberLabel": "45",
      "text": "Then came the officers to the chief priests and Pharisees; and they said unto them, Why have ye not brought him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:45",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:45"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-046",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 46,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:46",
      "numberLabel": "46",
      "text": "The officers answered, Never man spake like this man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:46",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:46"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-047",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 47,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:47",
      "numberLabel": "47",
      "text": "Then answered them the Pharisees, Are ye also deceived?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:47",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:47"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-048",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 48,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:48",
      "numberLabel": "48",
      "text": "Have any of the rulers or of the Pharisees believed on him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:48",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-049",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 49,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:49",
      "numberLabel": "49",
      "text": "But this people who knoweth not the law are cursed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:49",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:49"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-050",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 50,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:50",
      "numberLabel": "50",
      "text": "Nicodemus saith unto them, (he that came to Jesus by night, being one of them,)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:50",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:50"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-051",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 51,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:51",
      "numberLabel": "51",
      "text": "Doth our law judge any man, before it hear him, and know what he doeth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:51",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-052",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 52,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:52",
      "numberLabel": "52",
      "text": "They answered and said unto him, Art thou also of Galilee? Search, and look: for out of Galilee ariseth no prophet.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:52",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:52"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-053",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 53,
      "verseId": "kjv:john:7:53",
      "numberLabel": "53",
      "text": "And every man went unto his own house.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "John 7:53",
        "verseKey": "kjv:john:7:53"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "repository": "aruljohn/Bible-kjv",
